## Rotation

Change `rotation_trigger` to any new, non-secret value. The provider asks Pulse
to issue a successor credential and retires the unreachable predecessor under
Pulse's bounded overlap policy.

Do not place secret material in `rotation_trigger`; it is intentionally
non-sensitive and appears in plans.

## Drift behavior

If Pulse reports a credential version different from the version associated
with Terraform's stored secret, the provider clears the unusable secret, sets
`rotation_required`, and warns. Planning is blocked while `rotation_trigger`
is unchanged. Change it to a new value and apply; the provider never pretends
it can recover an old plaintext credential.

Deleting an automation-owned Terraform resource archives and disables the
integration; it does not hard-delete history. A human-owned integration must
first be explicitly adopted with `adopt = true`. This prevents a Terraform
destroy from bypassing the ownership transfer and credential rotation.

